+# mfa_ivector.loc.sample
+# This is a *.loc.sample file distributed with Galaxy that enables tools
+# to use a set of ivector model files. This one is for Montreal Forced Aligner (MFA).
+# See the wiki: http://wiki.galaxyproject.org/Admin/NGS%20Local%20Setup
+# First create these data files and save them in your own data directory structure.
+# Then, create a mfa_ivector.loc.sample file to use those models with tools.
+# Copy this file, save it with the same name (minus the .sample), 
+# follow the format examples, and store the result in this directory.
+# The file should include an one line entry for each index set.
+# The path points to the "basename" for the set, not a specific file.
+# It has four text columns seperated by TABS.
+# You can download and create the models using auxilary scripts provided in
+# "auxiliary_scripts" folder of this tool
+#
+# <value>	<dbkey>	<name>	<path>
+#
+# So, for example, if you had english_mfa model stored in:
+#
+#    /data/db/mfa/pretrained_models/ivector/
+#
+# containing *.zip models, such as:
+#
+#   -rw-r--r--. 1 armin armin 50411025 Dec  2 14:38 english_mfa.zip
+#
+# then the mfa_ivector.loc.sample entry could look like this:
+#
+#english_mfa	default	English (MFA)	/data/db/mfa/pretrained_models/ivector/english_mfa.zip
+#
+#Full example:
+#
+##<value>	<dbkey>	<name>	<path>
+#english_mfa	default	English (MFA)	/data/db/mfa/pretrained_models/ivector/english_mfa.zip
+#ivector_mfa	default	Ivector (MFA)	/data/db/mfa/pretrained_models/ivector/ivector_mfa.zip
+#multilingual_mfa	default	Multilingual (MFA)	/data/db/mfa/pretrained_models/ivector/multilingual_mfa.zip
